WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.880
Turn on a tap in Scotland,

2
00:00:01.880 --> 00:00:03.930
and your water comes from Scottish Water,

3
00:00:03.930 --> 00:00:06.030
which is publicly owned.

4
00:00:06.030 --> 00:00:09.450
Cross into England, and
private companies supply it.

5
00:00:09.450 --> 00:00:12.940
Water there was privatised in 1989.

6
00:00:12.940 --> 00:00:14.850
Two neighbours, the same good,

7
00:00:14.850 --> 00:00:17.890
and two different answers
to who should run it.

8
00:00:17.890 --> 00:00:21.270
So who decides what gets
made and who gets it:

9
00:00:21.270 --> 00:00:23.400
buyers and sellers, the government,

10
00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:25.620
or both? In this mission,

11
00:00:25.620 --> 00:00:30.280
you'll see how markets answer three
big questions every economy faces,

12
00:00:30.280 --> 00:00:32.230
and where they fall short.

13
00:00:32.230 --> 00:00:35.160
Then you'll compare the
private and public sectors:

14
00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:37.180
who owns them, who runs them,

15
00:00:37.180 --> 00:00:38.890
and what they aim for.

16
00:00:38.890 --> 00:00:41.580
Your mission: find out who decides,

17
00:00:41.580 --> 00:00:43.390
and weigh the case for each side.
